347	    <h2 class="section-title">Dataset Overview &amp; Historical Context</h2>
348	  </div>
349	  <div class="narrative">
350	    The Academy Award for Best Original Score has been presented annually since 1934, spanning <strong>93 ceremonies</strong> and honoring <strong>79 unique composers</strong>. From the orchestral grandeur of Max Steiner's Golden Age scores to the boundary-pushing work of contemporary artists like Hildur Guðnadóttir and Ludwig Göransson, the award has evolved from a celebration of Hollywood's European emigre tradition to a global recognition of musical innovation in cinema. This report analyzes every winner from <strong>1934 (Louis Silvers, One Night of Love)</strong> through <strong>2026 (Ludwig Göransson, Sinners)</strong>, identifying the composers, eras, and trends that have defined nearly a century of film music.
