omkin defined a lush, leitmotif-driven style. A handful of titans — Steiner, Tiomkin, Waxman, Rozsa — collected the bulk of repeat awards.',", "     'Silver Age (1960–1979)': 'A transitional period as the studio system dissolved and new voices emerged. Maurice Jarre\'s epic canvases, Henry Mancini\'s jazz-inflected melodies, and John Barry\'s sophisticated themes signaled diversification. The era closed with John Williams\' Star Wars, a bridge to blockbuster scoring.',", "     'Modern Era (1980–1999)': 'The blockbuster age. John Williams and Alan Menken dominated with a combined 7 wins across adventure, sci-fi, and Disney animation. Electronic and world-music influences entered via Vangelis, Herbie Hancock, and Tan Dun. The composer pool broadened significantly.',", "-    'Contemporary Era (2000–2026)': 'The most diverse era in Oscar scoring history. No single composer dominates. International voices (Tan Dun, A.R. Rahman, Gustavo Santaolalla), genre-bending artists (Trent Reznor & Atticus Ross), and global stars (Hans Zimmer, Alexandre Desplat) reflect the Academy\'s expanding sensibility. Ludwig Göransson\'s three wins across two decades underscore a new model of versatile, genre-fluid composition.'", "+    'Contemporary Era (2000–2026)': 'The most diverse era in Oscar scoring history. International voices (Tan Dun, A.R. Rahman, Gustavo Santaolalla), genre-bending artists (Trent Reznor & Atticus Ross), and global stars (Hans Zimmer, Alexandre Desplat) reflect the Academy\'s expanding sensibility. Ludwig Göransson\'s multiple wins across two decades underscore a new model of versatile, genre-fluid composition.'", " }", "-for e in era_data:", "-    desc = era_descriptions.get(e['era'], '')", "-    era_table_rows += (", "-        f"<tr><td>{e['era']}</td><td class='center'>{e['n_wins']}</td>"", "-        f"<td class='center'>{e['n_unique']}</td>"", "-        f"<td>{e['top_composer']} ({e['top_composer_wins']})</td>"", "-        f"<td class='center'>{e['repeat_rate']}